<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Waltons interim shr dives, no div.</title>
<headline>Waltons interim shr dives, no div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Aug 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib after exceps (cts) 5.9  vs  21.7</p>
<p>    Shr, headline (cts)	     15.0  vs  21.7</p>
<p>    Attrib income			5.75 vs  15.78</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			     15.47 vs  30.57</p>
<p>    Tax				    8.97 vs  11.46</p>
<p>    Interest paid		     24.30 vs  20.35</p>
<p>    Interest received		  9.44 vs   6.08</p>
<p>    Turnover			   743.43 vs 537.99</p>
<p>Full name: Waltons Stationery Company Ltd</p>
<p>    Share of associates'	     0.64 vs   0.86</p>
<p>    Exceptional items		 11.11 vs   -</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said that management has identified and formulated a plan of action to effectively deal with the controllable elements that have given rise to poor operating performance of the group in the six months under review. On the assumption that there will be no further deterioration in business conditions, the directors are of the opinion that the decline in earnings for the full financial period will be less than that reported in the first six months.</p>
<p>The group's policy is to declare a single dividend at year end.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
